  "Question": "What is the \\(100\\)th number in the arithmetic sequence \\(1,\\) \\(5,\\) \\(9,\\) \\(13,\\) \\(17,\\) \\(21,\\) \\(25,\\) \\(\\ldots?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(397\\)",
    "B": "\\(399\\)",
    "C": "\\(401\\)",
    "D": "\\(403\\)",
    "E": "\\(405\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Each term is \\(4\\) greater than the previous term. From the first term to the \\(100\\)th term there are \\(100-1=99\\) steps, so we add \\(4\\) a total of \\(99\\) times:\n\\[\n1+99\\cdot4=1+396=397.\n\\]\nThe \\(100\\)th number is \\(\\boxed{397}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
